                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the clean up! I do agree that the base dir has gotten cluttered but I'm not loving the idea of a directory for each app (it feels like we swung the pendulum all the way to the other side of things). Could we group them, maybe the main state apps (bmc, chassis, host, hypervisor) in one dir and then the other apps in their own dirs?\n\nAlso, I'd prefer the move to a static util library be a separate commit as it feels like a distinct change in itself."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Could we group them, maybe the main state apps (bmc, chassis, host, hypervisor) in one dir and then the other apps in their own dirs?\n\nSure, i can do that with the next revision.\n\n> Also, I'd prefer the move to a static util library be a separate commit as it feels like a distinct change in itself.\n\nRaised a separate change for the util libs:\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-state-manager/+/84498"
                },
                {
